From ef660d8f91df9470619506cde67d070970e1067a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:51:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 48/49] init: load persistent properties after the first
 encryption

"Encrypt tablet" encrypts /data in place and vold then carries on with
the same boot. ro.crypto.state was still unset at late-init, so init's
encrypted-device counter in load_persist_props skips the post-decrypt
call rather than the tmpfs one, and the user's persistent properties
stayed unloaded until the next boot: time zone, locale and the Bluetooth
address, without which the Bluetooth HAL aborted ("No Bluetooth
Address!", "Bluetooth keeps stopping"). Load them a second time on
vold's trigger; on other boots that re-reads the same values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016iwHzV2tPonTxdceSkWZtS
---
 rootdir/init.qcom.rc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rootdir/init.qcom.rc b/rootdir/init.qcom.rc
index dd60dcf..0678392 100644
--- a/rootdir/init.qcom.rc
+++ b/rootdir/init.qcom.rc
@@ -174,3 +174,11 @@ service qcom-post-boot /vendor/bin/init.qcom.post_boot.sh
     user root
     disabled
     oneshot
+
+# "Encrypt tablet" (FDE) encrypts in place and then vold carries on with the same boot. ro.crypto.state
+# was still unset at late-init, so init's encrypted-device counter in load_persist_props skips the
+# post-decrypt call instead of the tmpfs one, and the user's persistent properties (time zone, locale,
+# the Bluetooth address the BT HAL aborts without) stay unloaded until the next boot. A second load
+# right after vold's trigger covers that boot; on every other boot it re-reads the same values.
+on property:vold.decrypt=trigger_load_persist_props
+    load_persist_props
